{"title":"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equilateral_triangle\" title=\"Equilateral triangle\">equilateral triangle</a> is inscribed in the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ellipse\" title=\"Ellipse\">ellipse</a> whose equation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e539e0d96b18d417824e89c968df48666aa0b7aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+4y^2=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />. One vertex of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be11a56a55425d6c6b69f70f5fa98eab95e8ad18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, one altitude is contained in the y-axis, and the square of the length of each side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/904edb323df74efc69db571be3b334711f3c9340.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{m}{n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"40\" height=\"45\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(slightly_altered)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (slightly altered)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/c/c1c17659e426bf52cb1df3d3e5f87476ced5b24c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pointpen = black; pathpen = black + linewidth(0.7); path e = xscale(2)*unitcircle; real x = -8/13*3^.5; D((-3,0)--(3,0)); D((0,-2)--(0,2)); /* axes */ D(e); D(D((0,1))--(x,x*3^.5+1)--(-x,x*3^.5+1)--cycle); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"168\" /></center>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Denote the vertices of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/a/74ae5f3d2d5c9a0767f5fae081c4f77ee78f2d51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/737b15f20e17e7834a83b8188337bade510f22f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrant\" title=\"Quadrant\">quadrant</a> 4 and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is in quadrant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/0/93032f1ab8b685d84a767a2fde0d9006a464b5e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Note that the slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/9/e095550b61ad5835e2247d33ae437597225610f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan 60^\\circ = \\sqrt {3}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" /> Hence, the equation of the line containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/7/647cf5f03f729a69f551bc8dfd47692937940287.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y = x\\sqrt {3} + 1.\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />\nThis will intersect the ellipse when\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/a/30ab84862ba4b820e4390fe84ec03f7fa1bbb145.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*}4 = x^{2} + 4y^{2} &amp; = &amp; x^{2} + 4(x\\sqrt {3} + 1)^{2} \\\\ &amp; = &amp; x^{2} + 4(3x^{2} + 2x\\sqrt {3} + 1) \\implies x(13x+8\\sqrt 3)=0\\implies x = \\frac { - 8\\sqrt {3}}{13}. \\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"664\" height=\"70\" />\nWe ignore the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> solution because it is not in quadrant 3.\n</p><p>Since the triangle is symmetric with respect to the y-axis, the coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/f/88f7ffea68df43a29a472145f4e6ce91ab100505.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac {8\\sqrt {3}}{13},y_{0}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"86\" height=\"53\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d167cecaf0027056254ad25f9ee31a5cc382b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac { - 8\\sqrt {3}}{13},y_{0}\\right),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"111\" height=\"53\" /> respectively, for some value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d914fc5a4712576274f1da9b2cb6bf7e6009b10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_{0}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"11\" />\n</p><p>It is clear that the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9bed9ab9e3bc69f63f6469dce000f0d83c3fa38a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"11\" /> is irrelevant to the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Our answer is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c45bf9e9359d0e96f4355f720a38ab75d1a06f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BC = 2 \\cdot \\frac {8\\sqrt {3}}{13}=\\sqrt {4\\left(\\frac {8\\sqrt {3}}{13}\\right)^{2}} = \\sqrt {\\frac {768}{169}}\\implies m + n = \\boxed{937}.\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"63\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/6/9d65c8165448ca3c6ab60a21d7c230d6b832709e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y= -\\frac {\\sqrt{4-x^2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"118\" height=\"43\" />, so the two other points of the triangle are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d3974f066115dfbfdd93ea7b2ddadccd9bb74a71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,-\\frac {\\sqrt{4-x^2}}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"117\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/4/c34f8cb1ff659d5a3cb0777cdde9cd4c8e59e5d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-x,-\\frac {\\sqrt{4-x^2}}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"131\" height=\"43\" />, which are a distance of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> apart. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> equals the distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d3974f066115dfbfdd93ea7b2ddadccd9bb74a71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,-\\frac {\\sqrt{4-x^2}}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"117\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be11a56a55425d6c6b69f70f5fa98eab95e8ad18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, so by the distance formula we have \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/4/3f404ada52ae3f459f81b46c4137946683322286.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2x=\\sqrt{x^2+(\\frac {2-\\sqrt{4-x^2}}{2})^2}.\\]\" width=\"226\" height=\"53\" /> \n</p><p>Squaring both sides and simplifying through algebra yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/f/41ffa6836d8624b26ae100814fa0a6c562023228.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2= \\frac {192}{169}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"75\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd9571d7e7e3e2061d3f507ebd3b7707164fd645.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x=\\sqrt{\\frac{768}{169}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"95\" height=\"45\" /> and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/ccecc63cec35cde351656936435b28aec7627154.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{937}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_2_.28slightly_altered.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(slightly_altered)\">Solution 2 (slightly altered)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (slightly altered)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Instead of using the distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/4/0048145ffb6c9e5539adf5703a25157ee3e51553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,\\frac {\\sqrt{4-x^2}}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"103\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be11a56a55425d6c6b69f70f5fa98eab95e8ad18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, we use the distance between the midpoint of the base and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be11a56a55425d6c6b69f70f5fa98eab95e8ad18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>The midpoint of the base is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/4/12424bae2575326a441106b3533562721b7801cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,-\\frac {\\sqrt{4-x^2}}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"116\" height=\"43\" />, and the distance between the midpoint of the base and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be11a56a55425d6c6b69f70f5fa98eab95e8ad18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is equivalent to the height of the equilateral triangle: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00fc45eea294781fdd51408a9373e4b36eac70dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>So,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/6/fa66711cf800ebdf97ef1075dce8ea4b321c2e7d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {\\sqrt{4-x^2}}{2}+1=x\\sqrt{3}\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"40\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/0/9c08d409e2459712a4f72e543efa4b48b15b71ed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {\\sqrt{4-x^2}}{2}=x\\sqrt{3}-1\\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Squaring both sides:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/3/ef31a9a3b3dfce330ad96a0b7a90c92f15afeff4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {4-x^2}{4}=3x^2-2\\sqrt{3}x+1\\]\" width=\"198\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/4859e915791018047c42daa67a022ca10287195f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4-x^2=12x^2-8\\sqrt{3}x+4\\]\" width=\"206\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/b/8cbbce40573e0b1425428800a2df833d57b456f4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8\\sqrt{3}x=13x^2\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/2/49213e742fa7675ce6a4aab91d4c2fe004135a57.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=\\frac {8\\sqrt{3}}{13}\\]\" width=\"70\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49eb022b4f600f3f90aa01423aeb8f5d1b10f24c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac {8\\sqrt{3}}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"74\" height=\"43\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd9571d7e7e3e2061d3f507ebd3b7707164fd645.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x=\\sqrt{\\frac{768}{169}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"95\" height=\"45\" />, and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/a/0fac3153c855f0b0286e335e4e80cd69e2fbb010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$768+169=\\boxed{937}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"141\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~fibonaccispiralsofvitriol\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Since the altitude goes along the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> axis, this means that the base is a horizontal line, which means that the endpoints of the base are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/6/5e6440a4c7accf335cdfd1d7aa11f756c815d0a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />, and WLOG, we can say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is positive.\n</p><p>Now, since all sides of an equilateral triangle are the same, we can do this (distance from one of the endpoints of the base to the vertex and the length of the base):\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/2/112a9a2fdbc73adc9afddd382dd6ee4f5a55f36f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x^2 + (y-1)^2} = 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"163\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>Square both sides,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/5/3b51a3d490db3d6c67c3b8a530291fe83719dd15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + (y-1)^2 = 4x^2\\implies (y-1)^2 = 3x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"315\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Now, with the equation of the ellipse:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3ee81be30d0d31bb14f7454c0347084d02bec80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + 4y^2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/f/86f5b55518bdb8ed251116443dbcaa99471d5f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 = 4-4y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e972ee885cd153848c4b798ccd085347b5ebb35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x^2 = 12-12y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Substituting, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b55b666563baefe53c8ca00578ef27b9c42390f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12-12y^2 = y^2 - 2y +1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"188\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Moving stuff around and solving:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/7/667740f7660c3bdc8f094ccb41b463626f2dfeb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{-11}{13}, 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The second is found to be extraneous, so, when we go back and figure out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />  (which is the side length), we find it to be:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/7/457eab8aa6cfe1298259ba790c8ee4d66fe568b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{768}{169}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"49\" height=\"43\" /> \n</p><p>and so we get the desired answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/ccecc63cec35cde351656936435b28aec7627154.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{937}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be11a56a55425d6c6b69f70f5fa98eab95e8ad18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> as vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/1/0c1e22fe09c7388d738ebd1e52fb999e0eae620f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> as the vertex to the left of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> as the vertex to the right of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f1249ad95b7682b8316ad21de8ce4ee9fdcf93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/2/792daa030c96693198f143f9176bf888b7ca25cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C.$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> This implies\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/e/60eda1b55689cafffc33dec9eac3dff6018ca4d7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[C=\\left(x_0 , \\sqrt{\\frac{4-x_0^2}{4}}\\right)\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"53\" />\nand \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/2/12256d5491562a8ed63fc4bcc8a4de981f693238.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[B=\\left(-x_0 , \\sqrt{\\frac{4-x_0^2}{4}}\\right).\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"53\" />\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/1/ad1bf259771e5a5496e4c14c05fa9213b8920aaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=2x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"17\" /> and \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/1/211ac1bb3af9dba7819477d57af7e940e9465edd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{BC}{\\sqrt3}=AD=1-\\sqrt{\\frac{4-x_0^2}{4}}.\\]\" width=\"214\" height=\"47\" />\nThis yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/0/3507c2a2b91eac23a786c190c65590d23481ec26.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2x_0}{\\sqrt3}=1-\\sqrt{\\frac{4-x_0^2}{4}}.\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"47\" />\nRe-arranging and squaring, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/d/4adb9db571f848046869c9cc77980146265bc127.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{4-x_0^2}{4}=\\frac{4x_0^2}{3}-\\frac{4x_0}{\\sqrt3} +1.\\]\" width=\"194\" height=\"44\" />\nSimplifying and solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f1249ad95b7682b8316ad21de8ce4ee9fdcf93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/2/0c23fac472b9f3e8e530206154dbcc5de7b67d3d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_0=\\frac{48}{13\\sqrt 3}.\\]\" width=\"91\" height=\"41\" />\nAs the length of each side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/9/fb90223c0a2e803d40e2f22946a60b3139679142.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x_0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" /> our desired length is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/2/ce20e7c44b936625a87f2b9bba703ff2001fa8ac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4x_0^2=\\frac{768}{169}\\]\" width=\"80\" height=\"38\" />\nwhich means our desired answer is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/4/d14781ede36dc56e1189d985cd2261e456f5e410.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[768+169=\\boxed{937}\\]\" width=\"139\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~ASAB\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/6/60600e35891cc067b7b26fb71bb0bfb6255596ea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  import graph;    size(250);    pair A = (0,1);  pair B = (-8*sqrt(3)/13,-11/13);  pair C = (8*sqrt(3)/13,-11/13);    pair E = (0,-11/13);  pair O = (0,0);    // Ellipse x^2 + 4y^2 = 4  draw(ellipse((0,0),2,1));    // Triangle  draw(A--B--C--cycle);    // Median  draw(A--E);    // Dotted line from C to O  draw(C--O, dotted);    // Segment from origin to midpoint  draw(O--E);    // Labels  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, N);  label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SW);  label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, SE);  label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E + (0.15,0), SE);  label(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, SE);    // Points  dot(A);  dot(B);  dot(C);  dot(E);  dot(O);  // Axes  draw((-2.2,0)--(2.2,0));  draw((0,-1.2)--(0,1.1));  [/asy]\" width=\"418\" height=\"232\" /></center>\n<p><br />\n</p><p>We can begin by finding the length of line segment, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. On one hand, we can write, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/d/abd5d6cb6ca6bfad2943c2d12e87a711e724f27b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AE= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot AC=\\sqrt{\\frac{3m}{4n}}\\]\" width=\"192\" height=\"43\" /> as the altitude (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />) of an equilateral triangle is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9191a5007067cff8f6d73f4d3419e08238f00b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" /> multiplied by length of a side (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />). One the other hand we can also write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/8/d7823fc75ef4037076b523328f23204f6578c467.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AE=AO+OE\\]\" width=\"130\" height=\"14\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/b/1ebd082b1316ad51b461cf004b176dd29c7d7a91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,O,E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> are colinear. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c53cc93aa43cc55bea0dc2511833fe6bdda020f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> is the minor axis of the ellipse, it is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. From the equation of the ellipse, we also get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/a/10a8f79a71902801edf1996f89970a3c97c3550e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[EC^2+4\\cdot OE^2=4.\\]\" width=\"153\" height=\"17\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/4/30409b1d3f42213e20faa20d73be136bfd7869d5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[EC=\\frac{1}{2} BC=\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{m}{n}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{m}{4n}}\\]\" width=\"235\" height=\"43\" /> we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/4/0d4284db964d09139989457e755dcad7807f2c88.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\sqrt{\\frac{m}{4n}})^2+4\\cdot EO^2=4 \\implies 4\\cdot EO^2=4-\\frac{m}{4n}\\]\" width=\"362\" height=\"43\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/b/b7b491f2bda7709aa932e347f92638bd00b57a66.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[EO=\\sqrt{1-\\frac{m}{16n}}.\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"43\" /> Substituting this value back into the equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/957d4604acb3d6e0b31e32b6298e623a948dddbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=AO+OE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"133\" height=\"16\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/c/38c78c35d412d88483c0689a4fa41140c9fca2f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=1+\\sqrt{1-\\frac{m}{16n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"168\" height=\"45\" />. Because both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/4/d94792579432a22036155ebb8a1a35626d9e9a86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=\\sqrt{\\frac{3m}{4n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"101\" height=\"45\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/c/38c78c35d412d88483c0689a4fa41140c9fca2f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=1+\\sqrt{1-\\frac{m}{16n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"168\" height=\"45\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/2/d22d62bd16804d85af37606e3b53ae748a88413b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\frac{3m}{4n}}=1+\\sqrt{1-\\frac{m}{16n}}.\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"45\" /> Multiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/1/b417a127620d5b467fe7a48ad5f7d843e5c390b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, we get, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/8/708a53e7d5b3cd6849b57f3484e973db8ff0516b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{12mn}=4n+\\sqrt{16n^2-mn}.\\]\" width=\"230\" height=\"18\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/7/6d73897fc0bc0f5ea486a6b866a76b45aefc6b60.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{12mn}-4n=\\sqrt{16n^2-mn}.\\]\" width=\"230\" height=\"18\" /> Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/30260c50ffe8db04f128e373b1ca3d31f1f3707e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\sqrt{12mn}-4n)^2=(\\sqrt{16n^2-mn})^2\\]\" width=\"267\" height=\"21\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/3/6630439af3145197e8934bcfc62db5c1b8ff9ed9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[12mn+16n^2-8n\\sqrt{12mn}=16n^2-mn.\\]\" width=\"318\" height=\"18\" /> Canceling, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/1/f319284f49ae2ab05a7f46becf2d3342707434e5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[12mn-8n\\sqrt{12mn}=-mn.\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"18\" /> We can rewrite this as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/6/0761826f01ef66fa9dcd5df04ccb96ba81d10d17.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[13mn=8n\\sqrt{12mn}.\\]\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" /> Dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> gives us, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/c/6bc0b7edac16ec7a0154e797c22d1c901236a6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13m=8\\sqrt{12mn}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"21\" />. We can finally square both sides to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/2/312ac8a8270bd3263d09346e1701c8697b02d4eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$169m^2=768mn$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"17\" />. Dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/d/bcdeda420fd155657cef421a508e283b51a4bbbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$169m=768n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"14\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30bced5c282b8f0ac4d31aadc503684b2b6e7021.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{m}{n}=\\frac{768}{169}.\\]\" width=\"77\" height=\"38\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/3/e432253dc74df8658947140d23071a78d2e76897.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=768$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/9/ec96a7ae6809157b527dba0c63679b27f8d45614.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=169$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3d3b24dc1e7c0fdf9041b278c5527aeed2460ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n=768+169=\\boxed{937}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"215\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>~littleduckysteve\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e539e0d96b18d417824e89c968df48666aa0b7aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+4y^2=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" /> can be rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/2/f0271e32a3737395b493161ebf064709abb6df8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x)^2+(2y)^2=2^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"137\" height=\"21\" />. The points of the triangle are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/6457ca2dcd40dc21d9aa0db18c66bbac9af4d899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/1/d516037fd9d54de01b18c14d956e01c9d6b2a1dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-x, 1-x\\sqrt{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"24\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02bb45823af9ef06b6ac093f3aa5788bcfc02300.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, 1-x\\sqrt{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"24\" />. When plugging the second coordinate into the equation, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/f/22fe2af905817fe13405b3d0c67cb3c29bf7fd1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+4-8x\\sqrt{3}+12x^2=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"209\" height=\"21\" />, which equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/2/4e23b5647464db261f4fc5072168062363cb189d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13x^2-8x\\sqrt{3}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"21\" />. \n</p><p>This yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/0/4c0e147038c9c838a4ef54d06b8823047b2cf018.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(13x-8\\sqrt{3})=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"24\" />. Obviously x can't be 0, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/d/56d0821b3483d8e3068a944a14f5cdc5c5e0b81c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"74\" height=\"43\" />. The side length of the equilateral triangle is twice of this, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a1782544455b379d26bbc46b5f98110f86c79f4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{16\\sqrt{3}}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>This can be rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/c/4fc18e6390f00886ba756497817f4b1cd5395ba1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{256\\cdot3}{169}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{768}{169}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"146\" height=\"45\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/a/0fac3153c855f0b0286e335e4e80cd69e2fbb010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$768+169=\\boxed{937}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"141\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~ MC413551\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Consider the transformation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/a/c0ac9f06ea6d3de1c1a236da8b7ead0c62da511b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x/2, y).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> This sends the ellipse to the unit circle. If we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be one-fourth of the side length of the triangle, the equilateral triangle is sent to an isosceles triangle with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/f/1ef44b78dbce1ec374a0ddf2da52e73331ff453c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n, n\\sqrt{13}, n\\sqrt{13}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"23\" /> Let the triangle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11dea4f5b7f66cf564152a4ca6a6cd5d57091c76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=AC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" /> Let the foot of the altitude from A be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87fa832bf21ebc48a46289cd7aea73ffcc84c111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X.$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/e/bee3c97839b96517b435c417517ee889743409d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX=n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/e/f5eca8dea15e68abc80d853646de7478b6dd6635.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX=2n\\sqrt{3}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"21\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a point such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is a diameter of the unit circle. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/5/db578206f94b6a11147947450a7c33adc19aebe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XC=2-2n\\sqrt{3}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"21\" /> Using power of a point on X,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/f/fdf0c4133e5e5c50e6e92c8eaf38ca9f80231966.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2=2n\\sqrt{3}(2-2n\\sqrt{3})\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"21\" />\nSimplifying gets us to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/0/bf0e48278554c2398e1258fb949b91bfea776b58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13n^2=4n\\sqrt{3}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"21\" /> Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/f/6df8086e2e81481a950b06248d7305f09e6631be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=\\dfrac{4\\sqrt{3}}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"74\" height=\"43\" /> which means the side length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f4986756c50851cb8fd42ca21f28273626bd2902.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{16\\sqrt{3}}{13}=\\sqrt{\\dfrac{768}{169}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"127\" height=\"45\" />\nThus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/7/997985a5429c3b402b4576a2327c2d34aeae0c32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$768+169=\\boxed{937}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"146\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I\" title=\"2001 AIME I\">2001 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2001 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2001\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017194547\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.071 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.090 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 902/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1786/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 30025/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.579      1 -total\n 56.13%    7.061      1 Template:AIME_box\n 41.43%    5.212      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3064:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017194547 and revision id 288421. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}